entry.summary:
What is database replication? What is a replication issue? How do we solve the replication issues? 1. Managed Recovery Process (MRP) not running ALTER DATABASE RECOVER MANAGED STANDBY DATABASE DISCONNECT FROM SESSION;
Sometimes the MRP might be running but still replication fails. A restart of the database can also help solve this. SHUTDOWN IMMEDIATE; STARTUP MOUNT; ALTER DATABASE RECOVER MANAGED STANDBY DATABASE DISCONNECT FROM SESSION
2. Full archivelogs in the secondary database 3. Check for network issues 4. Listener issues ALTER SYSTEM REGISTER;
Conclusion Replication issues can sometimes cause you sleepless nights but with the right troubleshooting strategies, we can always overcome them. Have you encountered replication issues before? How did you overcome them? Feel free to share in the comments section how you solved them. In case you would like me to write about other database related topics, let me know too.
